    "reason": "The release note [ev-b8d6f16e3c8c] and PR #7549 [ev-aa93430c028a] say DNS01 issuance on Cloudflare broke because Cloudflare stopped returning zone IDs. The fix is limited to the Cloudflare DNS01 provider code (pkg/issuer/acme/dns/cloudflare) [ev-2c7ddbc1fc1f]. So the exposed environments are those whose ACME Issuer or ClusterIssuer uses a Cloudflare DNS01 solver. The proposal's two extra branches on spec.acme.dns01.providers[].cloudflare are not supported by any evidence. That legacy layout does not belong to the cert-manager.io API group, so I removed those branches and kept the solvers[] predicate. The evidence does not name the field path itself, so confidence is low.",
